1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,933
[CRICKETS CHIRPING]

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,500
What are you doing here?

3
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:15,267
Toto came by.

4
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:17,567
I can't believe you.

5
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:20,600
You're willing to throw
your own brother in jail.

6
00:00:23,667 --> 00:00:25,300
- You don't know anything--
- All I know is

7
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:26,367
you're filthy rich,

8
00:00:26,367 --> 00:00:28,667
but you're too stingy
to help your own brother!

9
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,167
[SCOFFS]

10
00:00:30,167 --> 00:00:31,633
Me, stingy?

11
00:00:32,733 --> 00:00:35,400
Ever since we were younger,
he's been addicted to gambling.

12
00:00:35,433 --> 00:00:37,467
He even gambled away
his tuition money.

13
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:40,400
When he got arrested,

14
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:42,267
I bailed him out right away.

15
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:45,300
I got him a job with Don Nato,
but what happened?

16
00:00:46,233 --> 00:00:48,167
He stole just
so he could gamble.

17
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:50,533
And what did I do?

18
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,500
Nothing...

19
00:00:53,533 --> 00:00:56,767
Because all I did
was defend my brother.

20
00:01:00,067 --> 00:01:02,367
I even got him a job
at Pindang Tocino,

21
00:01:02,367 --> 00:01:03,600
but he just wouldn't stop.

22
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:07,133
Every chance he got,
he'd take more and more.

23
00:01:07,733 --> 00:01:09,733
His gambling addiction
just kept getting worse.

24
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:12,667
So, June,
as much as it hurts me,

25
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:17,033
I have to let him face
the consequences.

26
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,500
Because I'm not the only one
affected by this.

27
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,533
Our employees will suffer too
if we go under because of him.

28
00:01:28,533 --> 00:01:30,033
So tell me, June...

29
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,667
am I really that terrible
of a brother?

30
00:01:35,667 --> 00:01:42,600
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

31
00:01:57,533 --> 00:02:04,467
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

32
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:15,600
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

33
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:17,733
There you go!

34
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,633
That's more like it.

35
00:02:19,633 --> 00:02:21,167
You should apologize
to me, June.

36
00:02:22,833 --> 00:02:24,100
[DOOR OPENS]

37
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:31,833
[MISCHIEVOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

38
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:34,367
W-What are you doing here?

39
00:02:34,767 --> 00:02:36,200
Are you okay?

40
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:39,867
I heard you two arguing.

41
00:02:40,333 --> 00:02:41,833
W-We're okay. Good night.

42
00:02:41,833 --> 00:02:43,367
W-Wait, Ping!

43
00:02:45,467 --> 00:02:47,233
[JUNE]<i> We're not having
</i> a lovers' quarrel anymore.

44
00:02:47,267 --> 00:02:48,733
<i> That was our first real fight.</i>

45
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,300
<i> Ugh!</i>

46
00:02:50,667 --> 00:02:52,033
<i> But Ima said,</i>

47
00:02:52,033 --> 00:02:54,600
<i> married couples shouldn't stay
mad at each other for too long.</i>

48
00:02:55,267 --> 00:02:57,267
<i> Are we a married couple?!</i>

49
00:02:58,667 --> 00:03:00,500
What happened to us?

50
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:04,933
We used to be very close.

51
00:03:04,933 --> 00:03:09,333
[MISCHIEVOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

52
00:03:09,333 --> 00:03:10,833
[JUNE]<i> Fine. I'll be the first
</i> to apologize

53
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:12,267
<i> since I started it anyway.</i>

54
00:03:12,267 --> 00:03:17,733
[MISCHIEVOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

55
00:03:17,733 --> 00:03:19,367
You cheaters!

56
00:03:19,367 --> 00:03:25,333
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]
